                                "text": "1907 (Mar.), L. F. Anderson, \"A Study of the Prototypes of the Modern Non-professional School among the Greeksand the Romans\", The Pedagogical Seminary, 14(1): 1-38.\nThe grammatist, apparently, taught literature in so far as it was read while the citharist taught the poetry which was usually sung."
